## The `Units.CGS` module of §8.20.
##
## The CGS units are ambient `Unit[d]` values from the kernel's unit table
## (§5.1); see `Units.SI`'s header for why no binding is declared here. The
## table itself: `dyn`, `erg`, `Gal`, `P`, `St`, `G` (gauss, `1/10000 T`),
## `Mx`, `Ba`, `Oe` (its scale carries `pi^-1`, §5.3.3).
module Units.CGS
